  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the interdisciplinary roles and responsibilities of an apprentice in the literary arts production;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Understanding The Roles and Responsibilities of an Apprentice in the Literary Arts Production: A. Literary arts within the publishing and print media industry B. Professionalism and ethics in literary arts; II. Organizational Requirements for Occupational Health and Safety in the Literary Arts Industry.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'discuss the different stages of literary arts production;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Stages In Literary Arts Production A. Manuscript preparation B. Pitching, contracting, and working with publishers C. Editorial work, designing, and printing D. Distribution, promotion, and advocating yourself as a writer'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'describe existing and emerging literary industries that contribute to the growth of the literary industry in the Philippines; and', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Different Literary Productions in the Philippine Context A. Books and bound formats B. Anthologies and collections C. Scripts for theater productions D. Screenplay for film and TV E. Digital media Projects F. Experimental and emerging formats V. Literary Arts as an Industry in the Philippines A. Publishers, productions, and other avenues for the literary arts in the Philippines B. Notable figures across literary genres C. Copyright and registration process D. Government agencies and the writing communities as systems of support'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'produce a literary analysis using the literary processes in writing based on understanding of literary genres, elements, and techniques; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, the learners may proceed to in-school or off-school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision and safety guidelines are observed.', NULL, NULL, 'VI. Writing Literary Analysis A. Considerations in text selection B. Methodologies in text analysis C. Contextualizing texts within publication nuances and social, cultural, and political contexts D. Strategies in literary analysis'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-005', 'demonstrate proficiency, professionalism, cultural, and ethical practices during internship or apprenticeship; and', NULL, NULL, 'Apprenticeship Proper'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-006', 'synthesize the internship or apprenticeship experience through creative documentation. social, cultural, and political contexts', NULL, NULL, 'Portfolio Development'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss media arts from the perspective of industry function and professional processes;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Media Arts and The Work Environment A. Review of media arts in the different creative industries domains B. Media arts and technology C. Narrative and visual storytelling in digital media D. Media arts as social commentary E. Role of the media artist in organizations and communities in the digital age F. Collaborative media production and industry networking G. Professional practice and entrepreneurial skills in media arts'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'articulate the professional roles and ethical practices of media artists in creative industry settings;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Professionalism and Ethics in Media Arts A. Professional practice in media arts production a. Standards and protocols in pre-production, production, and post-production b. Roles and responsibilities in collaborative media projects c. Documentation and workflow management in creative industries B. Ethical considerations in digital and media production a. Intellectual property rights and copyright law in media b. Representation, inclusivity, and cultural sensitivity in storytelling c. Truthfulness, transparency, and ethical editing practices C. Professional work ethics in media arts industries a. Integrity, accountability, and reliability in creative work b. Balancing artistic vision with organizational or industry standards c. Professional conduct in workplace and studio environments D. Client relations and commissioned media work'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'evaluate the roles, responsibilities, and accountability of apprentices in media arts organizations; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, the learners may proceed to in-school or off-school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision and safety guidelines are observed', NULL, NULL, 'III. Apprenticeship Orientation A. Roles and responsibilities of media arts apprentices B. Chain of accountability in apprenticeship settings C. Industry workplace expectations in media production D. Orientation prior to apprenticeship placement Note to the teacher: Conduct the orientation before the in-school or off- school apprenticeship.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'demonstrate proficiency and professionalism in media arts tasks and workplace practices during apprenticeship; and', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Apprenticeship Proper'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-005', 'synthesize apprenticeship experiences through creative documentation.', NULL, NULL, 'V. Portfolio Development A. Nature of apprenticeship and creative or media arts portfolios a. Purpose and role of portfolios in apprenticeship programs b. Types of creative portfolios (print, digital, multimedia) c. Standards and expectations in media arts portfolio presentation B. Components of a professional portfolio'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the interdisciplinary roles and responsibilities of dance artists and dance professionals, the functions of arts organizations, and the chain of accountability in dance production settings;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Understanding Dance Production, and the Dance Industry A. Orientation to the dance field 1. Core Elements of Dance Industry in Creative Industries ● Artistic Creation ● Production and Distribution ● Education and Skills Development ● Commercial Applications ● Cultural Preservation and Advocacy 2. Employment size and economic contributions of performing artists in the locality. II. Roles, Responsibilities, and Organizational Structures in Dance A. Roles and responsibilities of: • Dance artists • Choreographers • Production staff B. Functions of arts organizations (e.g., companies, institutions, cultural agencies) C. Chain of accountability in dance production: • Artistic Director • Choreographer • Production Manager • Performers and technical crew'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-002', 'explain the creative and work processes involved in dance production;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Work Process in Dance Production: A. Concept and creative development B. Rehearsal process C. Technical preparation D. Dress rehearsals E. Performance F. Post-performance evaluation and reflection'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-003', 'practice safety and security procedures related to the dance, including physical and emotional wellbeing;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Organizational Requirements for Occupational Health and Safety in the Dance Industry. A. Workplace safety requirements B. Types of workplace hazards C. Nutrition for dancers, D. Anatomy of dancers E. Physical and emotional wellbeing in dance practice'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how professional, corporate social responsibility, and ethical practices can be applied in the dance industry; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, the learners may proceed to in-school or off-school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision, documentation, and safety procedures are observed.', NULL, NULL, 'V. Professionalism in the Dance Industry A. Skill development and education B. Respectful work environment C. Punctuality and accountability D. Ethical artistic decision-making VI. Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) in Dance A. Community engagement B. Diversity and inclusion C. Environmental sustainability D. Support for marginalized communities VII. Ethical Practices in Dance A. Fair compensation and working conditions B. Respect for cultural ownership C. Transparent decision-making D. Ethical representation'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-005', 'demonstrate proficiency, professionalism, ethical practice, and respect for the culture of the dance organization or institution as expected of apprentices; and', NULL, NULL, 'VIII. Apprenticeship Proper A. Technique development or hands-on training B. Production work C. Dance appreciation series'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Dance', 12, 'G12-006', 'synthesize the apprenticeship experience through creative documentation.', NULL, NULL, 'IX. Portfolio Development A. Rehearsal reports B. Performance reports'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss safety and security procedures in the music;', NULL, NULL, 'A. Organizational requirements for occupational health and safety in the music industry. 1. Workplace Safety Requirements 2. Types of Workplace Hazards 3. Nutrition for Musicians 4. Anatomy for Musicians'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-002', 'discuss the interdisciplinary roles and responsibilities of music artists, the functions of art organizations, and chain of accountability in the organization as an apprentice;', NULL, NULL, 'B. Understanding Music Production, the Profession, and Professionalism in the Arts 1. Orientation to the specific art field or discipline a. Music Industry structure • Recording Industry • Digital Music Distribution • Music Publishing Industry • Artist Management • Music Practitioners (Teaching Artists) b. Employment size and economic contributions of performing artists in the locality.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-003', 'explain the work process involved in music production and related performing arts field;', NULL, NULL, 'C. Work Processes in Music Production and Performance 1. Stages of music production: • Pre-production, • Production, and • Post-production 2. Workflow in performance and production settings 3. Collaboration among artists and production teams'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how professional, corporate social responsibility, and ethical practices can be applied in the music industry; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, learners may proceed to in-school or off- school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision, documentation, and safety procedures are observed.', NULL, NULL, 'D. Professionalism and ethics in the music industry; 1. Roles and responsibilities as a member of a group of musicians. 2. Artist treatment and compensation.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-005', 'demonstrate proficiency, professionalism, cultural sensitivity, and ethical practices under music apprenticeship; and', NULL, NULL, 'D. Music Apprenticeship Proper 1. Types of Music Apprenticeship Models a. Conservatory Model b. Traditional Philippine indigenous school of living traditions Model c. Popular Musicians Model 2. Methods and Strategies a. Notation-based learning b. Collaborative learning through Peers c. Observation-based through demonstration and recordings d. Improvisation'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Music', 12, 'G12-006', 'synthesize the music apprenticeship experience through creative documentation.', NULL, NULL, 'E. Portfolio Development 1. Showcase Portfolio 2. Developmental Portfolio'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the interdisciplinary roles and responsibilities of theater artists, the functions of art organizations, and the chain of accountability in the organization as an apprentices;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Organizational Structure and Roles in Theater Production A. Roles and responsibilities of theater artists and the chain of accountability in the theater organization B. Types and functions of theater organizations; and C. Processes and practices in theater productions and theater organizations.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'explain the work process involved in theater production and related performing arts field;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Organizational Structure and Roles in Theater Production A. Roles and responsibilities of theater artists and the chain of accountability in the theater organization B. Types and functions of theater organizations; and C. Processes and practices in theater productions and theater organizations.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'practice safety and security procedures in the theater arts practice;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Organizational Requirements for Occupational Health and Safety in the Theater Industry A. Workplace and safety requirements B. Types of workplace hazards C. Nutrition for Theater Artists D. Anatomy for Theater Artists'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how professionalism, corporate social responsibility, and ethical practices are applied in the theater industry; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, the learners may proceed to in-school or off-school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision, documentation, and safety procedures are observed.', NULL, NULL, 'III. Professionalism and Ethics in the theater industry A. Roles and responsibilities as a participant in a theater production and/or member of a theater organization B. Ethical practices in the theater industry C. Terms of reference and compensation.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss conceptual and cultural foundations of Traditional Cultural Expressions;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Conceptual and Cultural Foundations of Traditional Cultural Expressions A. Conceptual and cultural exploration of Traditional Cultural Expressions B. Traditional arts as expressions of community identity and heritage C. Narrative traditions and cultural storytelling through traditional arts D. Traditional arts as cultural and social commentary E. Role of cultural practitioners and tradition bearers in communities F. Collaborative cultural practices and community engagement G. Identification of the relevant creative industry domain of the project.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-002', 'explain professional roles and practices of cultural practitioners in Traditional Cultural Expressions;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Professionalism and Ethics in Traditional Cultural Expressions A. Professional practice in community-based traditional arts B. Ethical considerations in the practice and transmission of traditional arts C. Cultural sensitivity and respect for indigenous knowledge systems D. Client relations, commissions, and cultural production E. Cultural sustainability and community partnerships'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-003', 'analyze ethical and cultural practices in Traditional Cultural Expressions production;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Ethical And Cultural Practices in Traditional Cultural Expressions Production A. Ethical practices in cultural production B. Respect for cultural ownership and intellectual property of communities C. Cultural protocols and permissions in artistic production D. Professional conduct in collaborative community art practices'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-004', 'evaluate the roles, responsibilities, and accountability of apprentices in Traditional Cultural Expressions; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, learners may proceed to an in-school or off-school apprenticeship, provided that proper supervision and community coordination are ensured.', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Apprenticeship Orientation A. Roles and responsibilities of apprentices in cultural practice settings B. Chain of accountability in apprenticeship and community partnerships C. Expectations in working with cultural practitioners and community groups D. Orientation prior to apprenticeship placement'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-005', 'demonstrate proficiency in assigned tasks and professionalism in workplace behavior during apprenticeship in Traditional Cultural Expressions; and', NULL, NULL, 'V. Apprenticeship Proper'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Traditional Cultural Expressions', 12, 'G12-006', 'synthesize apprenticeship experiences through cultural documentation.', NULL, NULL, 'VI. Portfolio Development'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss conceptual and theoretical approaches in visual art practice and production;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Conceptual and Theoretical Foundations in Visual Art A. Conceptual and theoretical exploration of visual art practices ● Artist (Creator) ● Artwork (The work itself) ● World (Context/Time) ● Audience (Viewer/Interpreter) B. Function of Art ● Art and visual storytelling ● Art as social commentary ● Art as a profession C. Role of the Visual Artist in the Social Organization and Community D. Professional Practice and Entrepreneurial Skills in Visual Arts E. Collaborative Art Practices and Industry Networking'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'analyze professional and ethical practices in visual art production; NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTATION: If the orientation and preparatory competencies are completed within the first weeks of the term, learners may proceed to in- school or off-school apprenticeship activities, provided that proper supervision and safety guidelines are observed.', NULL, NULL, 'II. Professionalism and Ethics in Visual Arts A. Professional practices in visual art production B. Ethical considerations in art production C. Professional work ethics in creative industries D. Contract, client relations and commissioned works E. Art funding and project opportunities'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'evaluate the roles, responsibilities, and accountability of apprentices in visual art organizations;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Apprenticeship Orientation A. Roles and responsibilities of visual art apprentices B. Chain of accountability in apprenticeship settings C. Industry workplace expectations D. Orientation prior to apprenticeship placement'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'demonstrate proficiency and professionalism during visual arts apprenticeship; and', NULL, NULL, 'VII. Apprenticeship Proper Note: Use a task log sheet to document daily activities signed by the immediate supervisor.'),
  ('Arts Apprenticeship - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-005', 'synthesize apprenticeship experiences through creative documentation.', NULL, NULL, 'VIII. Portfolio Development'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-001', 'explain design thinking as a human-centered, structured, non-linear, and iterative approach to solving real-world problems.', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-002', 'differentiate design thinking from other research- informed outputs such as project-making, research reporting, invention, and business planning.', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-003', 'describe the phases of the design thinking process: empathy, sense-making, ideation, prototyping, testing, and reflection.', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze examples of real services, products, or other innovations that used the design thinking process.', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-005', 'identify the ethical responsibilities of designers when working with people and communities, including - obtaining informed consent', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-006', 'identify the ethical responsibilities of designers when working with people and communities, including - demonstrating respect for individuals and cultural diversity', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-007', 'identify the ethical responsibilities of designers when working with people and communities, including - safeguarding privacy and confidentiality', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-008', 'identify the ethical responsibilities of designers when working with people and communities, including - ensuring safety and inclusive participation', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-009', 'identify the ethical responsibilities of designers when working with people and communities, including - preventing potential harm throughout the design process. understanding of … methods for understanding problems through the lived experiences, behaviors, needs, emotions, and environments of users and communities.', NULL, NULL, 'Foundations of Human-Centered Design and Innovation (Mga Batayan ng Disenyong Nakasentro sa Tao at Inobasyon)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-010', 'identify a possible area of concern in the school, community, workplace, or chosen field, using environmental scanning or other similar methods.', NULL, NULL, 'Listening to Users and Understanding Contexts (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-011', 'evaluate the team''s current knowledge, underlying assumptions, gaps, and information needs related to the identified area of concern to guide further inquiry.', NULL, NULL, 'Listening to Users and Understanding Contexts (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-012', 'analyze the key users and stakeholders in the identified area of concern and the significance of their perspectives.', NULL, NULL, 'Listening to Users and Understanding Contexts (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-013', 'use ethical and respectful inquiry methods such as kuwentuhan, field observations, surveys, anino, and expert consultations to gather relevant information about key users and stakeholders, and the identified area of concern.', NULL, NULL, 'Listening to Users and Understanding Contexts (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-014', 'document users'' stories, behaviors, challenges, constraints, and opportunities as bases for generating appropriate design solutions. processes and mental models for organizing design research, identifying patterns, and reframing broad concerns into actionable design challenges.', NULL, NULL, 'Listening to Users and Understanding Contexts (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-015', 'analyze user data to identify patterns, tensions, needs, and opportunities derived from community stories and observations.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking and Problem Framing (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-016', 'examine how different users experience a problem by considering their perspectives and reframing the situation from their points of view.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking and Problem Framing (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-017', 'generate evidence-based insights explaining users'' needs, challenges, and underlying reasons based on community data and context.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking and Problem Framing (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-018', 'construct a design challenge or problem statement by synthesizing feedback from community understanding of … members, peers, teachers, and experts.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking and Problem Framing (Himayin ang Konteksto)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-019', 'explain why the selected design challenge or problem statement is meaningful, actionable, and well-defined based on the users'' needs, insights, and context. framing presentation. collaborative ideation methods that generate many possible responses to a design challenge before selecting ideas for testing.', NULL, NULL, 'DOMAIN'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-020', 'generate multiple ideas to address the design challenge using different structured ideation methods, such as bukas-daloy-sarado, use cases and Substitute-Combine-Adapt-Modify-Out to another use-Eliminate-Reverse (SCAMPER) model.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-021', 'facilitate collaborative sessions with users or community members identified area of concern.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-022', 'develop solution ideas by building on, combining, and improving others'' contributions during the collaborative ideation.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-023', 'synthesize ideas to identify patterns, similarities, relationships, and promising directions for further development.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-024', 'apply constructive feedback practices in critique sessions as both giver and receiver.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-025', 'generate clear criteria such as context fit, feasibility, desirability, accessibility, ethics, safety, sustainability, and relevance to select, and refine ideas.', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-026', 'develop selected ideas into clear solution concepts responsive to user needs and contextual constraints. prototyping as a quick, low-cost, visual, physical, or experiential way to test assumptions', NULL, NULL, 'Co-Design and ideation (Ambagan ng mga Ideya)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-027', 'explain the value of early prototyping in testing ideas and learning from feedback.', NULL, NULL, 'Making Ideas Testable (Bumuo ng Prototype)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-028', 'construct prototypes using available and appropriate materials.', NULL, NULL, 'Making Ideas Testable (Bumuo ng Prototype)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-029', 'identify assumptions to be tested through the understanding of … and learn from users. prototype.', NULL, NULL, 'Making Ideas Testable (Bumuo ng Prototype)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-030', 'gather preliminary feedback on prototypes from peers, teachers, and selected users.', NULL, NULL, 'DOMAIN'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-031', 'document feedback and proposed improvements to refine the prototype and guide further development. prototypes, or physical prototypes. feedback gathering as a respectful, structured, and human-centered process for determining whether a prototype responds to actual needs and experiences.', NULL, NULL, 'DOMAIN'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-032', 'conduct user or community testing through collaborative activities such as testing sessions, gallery walk, and sama-sama scoring.', NULL, NULL, 'User Testing and Feedback gathering (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-033', 'observe how users interact with the prototype and document their actions, reactions, questions, points of confusion, and difficulties encountered.', NULL, NULL, 'User Testing and Feedback gathering (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-034', 'collect feedback from diverse users and stakeholders regarding the usability, effectiveness, and relevance of the prototype, including those who experience the problem differently.', NULL, NULL, 'User Testing and Feedback gathering (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-035', 'document feedback accurately without dismissing inconvenient or critical comments. evaluation in design as the process of interpreting feedback, identifying necessary improvements, and making justified design decisions.', NULL, NULL, 'User Testing and Feedback gathering (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-036', 'organize and analyze feedback to identify patterns, priorities, actionable insights, tensions, gaps, and unresolved questions.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking, Evaluation, and Design Decisions (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-037', 'evaluate prototypes using established criteria such as context fit, feasibility, desirability, accessibility, ethics, safety, sustainability, and relevance.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking, Evaluation, and Design Decisions (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-038', 'explain trade-offs in design decisions by describing how different user needs are balanced, prioritized, or adjusted.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking, Evaluation, and Design Decisions (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-039', 'refine prototypes based on user understanding of … feedback, reflections, and evaluation results. communication and reflection as integral to design work, demonstrating both process and learning beyond final outputs.', NULL, NULL, 'Sensemaking, Evaluation, and Design Decisions (Ipakita, Suriin, at Ayusin)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-040', 'prepare a comprehensive capstone project report documenting the design and innovation process, including problem framing, ideation, prototyping, testing, and refinement.', NULL, NULL, 'Capstone Communication, Reflection, Portfolio (Komunikasyon, Pagninilay, at Portfolio sa Capstone)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-041', 'present the capstone project using clear, organized, and audience-appropriate visual and oral communication strategies.', NULL, NULL, 'Capstone Communication, Reflection, Portfolio (Komunikasyon, Pagninilay, at Portfolio sa Capstone)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-042', 'defend the capstone project by explaining its design, decisions, process, and outcomes before an audience or evaluation panel.', NULL, NULL, 'Capstone Communication, Reflection, Portfolio (Komunikasyon, Pagninilay, at Portfolio sa Capstone)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-043', 'explain ethical, social, environmental, and sustainability considerations addressed in the project.', NULL, NULL, 'Capstone Communication, Reflection, Portfolio (Komunikasyon, Pagninilay, at Portfolio sa Capstone)'),
  ('Design and Innovation', 12, 'G12-044', 'reflect on the design and innovation process to identify key learnings, strengths, limitations, and areas for improvement. understanding of …', NULL, NULL, 'Capstone Communication, Reflection, Portfolio (Komunikasyon, Pagninilay, at Portfolio sa Capstone)'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the purpose and requirements of Field Exposure', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 1 A. Brief Overview of Career Pathways B. Orientation with Partner Industry and other Work Settings 1. Professional Environments 2. Organizational Structure (Hierarchy, Roles, and Responsibilities) 3. Workplace Culture, Dynamics, and Expectations 4. Workplace Practices and Professional Standards'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-002', 'analyze how employee behaviors, workplace interactions, and organizational practices influence organizational effectiveness', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 1 A. Brief Overview of Career Pathways B. Orientation with Partner Industry and other Work Settings 1. Professional Environments 2. Organizational Structure (Hierarchy, Roles, and Responsibilities) 3. Workplace Culture, Dynamics, and Expectations 4. Workplace Practices and Professional Standards'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-003', 'apply reflective practice to analyze workplace experiences and learning gained from field exposure', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 1 A. Brief Overview of Career Pathways B. Orientation with Partner Industry and other Work Settings 1. Professional Environments 2. Organizational Structure (Hierarchy, Roles, and Responsibilities) 3. Workplace Culture, Dynamics, and Expectations 4. Workplace Practices and Professional Standards'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze the realities of practice and complexities of workplace interactions', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 2 Off-Campus Field Exposure Proper (Workplace Readiness Application) • Workplace Observation • Professional Interaction • Conduct of Interviews • Employability Skills Observation • Field Exposure Documentation'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-005', 'observe workplace culture, organizational practices, and professional standards demonstrated in authentic workplace settings', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 2 Off-Campus Field Exposure Proper (Workplace Readiness Application) • Workplace Observation • Professional Interaction • Conduct of Interviews • Employability Skills Observation • Field Exposure Documentation'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-006', 'demonstrate professionalism, ethical conduct, and appropriate workplace behavior during field exposure activities', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 2 Off-Campus Field Exposure Proper (Workplace Readiness Application) • Workplace Observation • Professional Interaction • Conduct of Interviews • Employability Skills Observation • Field Exposure Documentation'),
  ('Field Exposure (Off-Campus)', 12, 'G12-007', 'synthesize workplace observations to assess one''s readiness and preparedness for future career pathways', NULL, NULL, 'PHASE 3 Post Off-Campus Field Exposure Activity A. Field Exposure Debriefing B. Field Exposure Evaluation C. Career Action Plan Validation D. Action Plan Presentation and Reflection'),
